{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_rate_safestan`, a deterministic top-level copy of the originally scored expression `to_vector(y) ./ to_vector(n)`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_rate_safestan` to the data block so the likelihood left-hand side is a plain protected top-level identifier, as required by SafeStan. In `data_safe.json`, `y_rate_safestan[j] = y[j] / n[j]` for each `j`. Reordered the parameter prior sampling statements to occur before any model-block use of those parameters. The likelihood and posterior density are otherwise preserved.","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int J;
  array[J] int n;
  vector[J] x;
  array[J] int y;
  vector[J] y_rate_safestan;
  real r;
  real R;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_theta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_distance;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  real<lower=0> overshot;
  real<lower=0> distance_tolerance;
}
model {
  vector[J] p_angle;
  vector[J] p_distance;
  vector[J] p;

  sigma_theta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_distance ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  overshot ~ normal(1, 5);
  distance_tolerance ~ normal(3, 5);

  p_angle = 2 * Phi(asin((R - r) ./ x) / sigma_theta) - 1;
  p_distance = Phi((distance_tolerance - overshot)
                   ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance))
               - Phi((-overshot) ./ ((x + overshot) * sigma_distance));
  p = p_angle .* p_distance;
  y_rate_safestan ~ normal(p,
                           sqrt(p .* (1 - p) ./ to_vector(n)
                                + sigma_y ^ 2));
}
generated quantities {
  real sigma_degrees;
  sigma_degrees = (180 / pi()) * sigma_theta;
}
